Host semantic checks for the ARM64 BPF atomic emitter
===================================================
Run with TEST_OUTPUT pointing outside the kernel source tree:
  TEST_OUTPUT=/absolute/output python3 tools/testing/selftests/bpf_arm64_atomics/run-host.py

Requires GCC and AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. The runner extracts
actual LL/SC emission code and register mapping. A small instruction-semantics
model checks 21,840 combinations of 32/64-bit arithmetic/bitwise/fetch/exchange/
compare-exchange, positive/negative/zero offsets, source/destination registers,
comparison success/failure and a failed store-exclusive retry. It verifies old
value returns, updated memory, zero extension and preserved BPF registers.

This does not execute ARM64 machine code or the kernel verifier. It does not
validate real concurrency, instruction encodings or LSE operations (the target
configuration disables LSE). Full kernel build and live verifier/atomic/network/
accounting tests remain necessary. Source hash and sanitizer result are retained.

The companion test-live.c is a bounded native diagnostic for authorized rooted
Android tests. It loads unattached socket filters, runs each once using
BPF_PROG_TEST_RUN and closes every descriptor. It checks 40 arithmetic/fetch/
exchange/compare-exchange executions plus invalid opcode, unaligned address and
invalid-width rejection. It also performs1,024 concurrent map increments and checks unique old values.
The temporary map and program descriptors are closed; no pins or attachments persist.
It does not replace concurrent-operation or unprivileged-policy testing.
Compile against the Android Bionic/UAPI headers; do not bundle it in the ROM.
